- helm
- net
- mesa_foot

' The packet pump of the foot at /io/mesa: the actor that waits on the
' socket, and the loop that runs the foot's rules. The pump:
' - takes packets off the socket and gives them to the rules
' - sends the packets the rules make (hints); the engine sends its own
'   packets through the socket
' - tells the rules the time when the engine needs it, and at least once a
'   second
' - asks the world to make each change the rules ask for, one at a time
'   (mesa_wire/wish)
' - writes the mark before it announces a new epoch; if the mark is not
'   written, it announces nothing
' - tells Mesa the key each card names for a peer; Mesa decides whether to
'   accept it and keeps what it accepted
'
' Nothing here decides anything about a page: the rules are in mesa_foot
' and net. Nothing here holds a private key: Mesa holds the world's key and
' the key it accepted for each peer.
'
' The foot's record, /<self>/io/mesa, holds:
' - `port`: where the foot listens
' - `ring`: the file of the world's key (32 bytes that only Mesa reads)
' - `mark`: the file of the mark (the rift, the highest epoch announced,
'   and the lowest key manifest revision the world accepts)
' - `life`: the number of the world's key; a higher number makes the foot
'   change to a new key
'
' These files are in the world's folder, in io/mesa/, and not in its store:
' - the mark
' - the key file, and one more for each later key (`ring.2`, ...)
' - `ring.manifest`: which key Mesa signs with for the world
' - `ring.authority`: what Mesa accepted for each peer, and each block
'
' A restore of the store does not roll them back. So a restore is noticed
' (the mark), an old key of the world is not used again (the manifest), and
' a peer key that Mesa replaced or blocked is not accepted again (the
' authority).
'
' The card of a peer, /<self>/io/mesa/<peer>, holds the `key` this world
' wants Mesa to accept for that peer, its `life` and `rift` (1 and 0 when
' absent), and the `host` and `port` where the peer is reached. A card is a
' request. If Mesa refuses it, the foot writes the reason beside the card
' (`stand`) and the peer is not a peer of the foot.
'
' Packets travel as UDP datagrams on one socket. The socket tells which
' peer a packet is from by its source address, and drops a packet from an
' address no card names. The address is not trusted: Mesa checks every
' page against the key it accepted.
'
' The foot stops when its record is removed or holds `stop`. It stops the
' waiting actor, closes the socket and the engine, and ends.
+ mesa_wire
  + tick
    ' What the waiting actor tells the foot. `serial` is the number of the
    ' socket it waits on. `ready` is 1 when the socket holds a packet, 0 when
    ' the time ran out, and 2 when the socket is closed.
    : now=nat serial=nat ready=nat
  + again
    ' The foot asks itself for a new engine (mesa_foot/effect/renew).
    : era=nat
  + task
    & feet/task/ack
      feet/task/fact
      feet/task/binary
      mesa_wire/tick
      mesa_wire/wish
      mesa_wire/again
  + wish
    ' A change that part of the foot asks the world to make (mesa_foot/change).
    ' The foot sends it to its own mailbox, so any part can ask and the loop
    ' makes one change at a time.
    '
    ' A write to this world is one poke. A landing is planned on the world as
    ' it is when its turn comes (mesa_wire/ask, mesa_wire/plan) and is then one
    ' land command. The foot asks for nothing else until the answer comes, so
    ' each answer belongs to the first wish in the queue.
    : request=nat change=mesa_foot/change
  + whole
    ' The read that gives the world as it is now. A committed world is in the
    ' store, so handing it over copies no data.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ [nat any nat]
    [200 state 0]
  + world
    ' Gives the answer of mesa_wire/whole its type.
    \ body=any
    ^ namespace
    body
  + look
    ' Asks the supervisor for the world as it is now.
    \ parent=nat
    ^ nat
    | Send parent (feet/gift/snapshot_bat 0 mesa_wire/whole)
  + ask
    ' Starts the first wish in the queue, if there is one. A write is sent as
    ' it is. For a landing it first asks for the world as it is now, with
    ' request number 1: the landing is planned on that world (mesa_wire/plan).
    \ parent=nat queue=row[mesa_wire/wish]
    ^ nat
    ? !(queue.len) 0
    ? queue.at(0).change
     > (./write target change) (Send parent (feet/gift/poke target change))
     > (./land root card epic) (Send parent (feet/gift/snapshot_bat 1 mesa_wire/whole))
  + plan
    ' Runs when the world arrives for the landing at the front of the queue.
    ' It plans the landing on that world (net/land) and sends the plan as one
    ' land command. If the rules refuse the epic there is no command, and the
    ' reason is the answer to the wish.
    \ parent=nat queue=row[mesa_wire/wish] state=namespace
    ^ maybe[iota]
    = none=maybe[iota] .none
    ? !(queue.len) none
    ?> (./land root card epic) queue.at(0).change none
    ? (net/land root card epic state)
     > (./err why) (./some why)
     > (./ok made)
      ; (Send parent (feet/gift/land root.at(0) made.base made.diffs made.writes))
      none
  + note
    ' The wish that pokes a record on the foot's node.
    \ home=path word=myth
    ^ mesa_wire/wish
    | mesa_wire/wish 0 (mesa_foot/change/write home (writ/poke word))
  + waiter
    ' Waits on the foot's socket. It tells the foot when the socket holds a
    ' packet or when the time the foot gave it has passed. Then it waits for
    ' the foot's answer: how many milliseconds to wait next, or 0 to stop. A
    ' socket is a number, so this actor can wait on a socket the foot owns.
    \ fd=nat serial=nat self=nat
    ^ nat
    = ;[hello caps] (Recv[nat] 0)
      foot caps.at(0)
    % wait=nat 1
    = ;ready (MesaWait fd wait)
    ; (? (eq 2 ready) (Sleep 1) 0)
    ; (SendCaps foot (mesa_wire/tick (div (Now 0) 1000000) serial ready) [0])
    = ;[go more] (Recv[nat] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps more)
    ? !(go) 0
    | _ go
  + watch
    ' Starts the waiter of a socket.
    \ fd=nat serial=nat
    ^ nat
    = ;helper (Spawn (mesa_wire/waiter fd serial))
    ; (SendCaps helper 0 [0])
    0
  + route
    ' A peer as its card gives it: the key this world wants Mesa to accept for
    ' the peer, its life and rift, and the address where the peer is reached.
    : world=iota id=nat key=nat life=nat rift=nat host=str port=nat
  + routes
    ' The peers a binding names: each child that holds a key and an address.
    \ binding=axal[saga]
    ^ row[mesa_wire/route]
    = none=row[mesa_wire/route] []
    | binding.kid_tap.fold none
      \ out=row[mesa_wire/route] [key tree]
      ^ row[mesa_wire/route]
      ?> (./some version) tree.fil out
      = card (unpin version.myth)
        held card.nat_at(['key] 0)
        port card.nat_at(['port] 0)
      ? (eq 0 held) out
      ? (eq 0 port) out
      | out.snoc((mesa_wire/route key (quip_val key) held card.nat_at(['life] 1) card.nat_at(['rift] 0) card.txt_at(['host]) port))
  + own
    \ binding=axal[saga]
    ^ myth
    ?> (./some version) binding.fil myth/new
    | unpin version.myth
  + link
    ' What the foot holds of a peer:
    ' - the card Mesa accepted (key 0: Mesa accepted none, or the card is gone)
    ' - the peer's numeric address (0: none)
    ' - the generation of its route, which is also the number the engine knows
    '   the route by
    '
    ' The generation only goes up, so the foot keeps the link of a peer whose
    ' card is gone.
    : world=iota id=nat key=nat life=nat rift=nat host=str port=nat address=nat gen=nat
  + peers
    ' The peers of the foot: the links Mesa accepted a key for.
    \ links=row[mesa_wire/link]
    ^ row[mesa_foot/peer]
    = none=row[mesa_foot/peer] []
    | links.fold none
      \ out=row[mesa_foot/peer] item=mesa_wire/link
      ^ row[mesa_foot/peer]
      ? (eq 0 item.key) out
      | out.snoc((mesa_foot/peer item.world item.id))
  + why
    ' The reason the kernel gave for refusing a poke, or none if it accepted.
    \ err=maybe[pail]
    ^ maybe[iota]
    = none=maybe[iota] .none
      unknown=iota 'net_refused
    ?> (./some refusal) err none
    ?> (./some said) (pail/as[helm/supervisor/rejection] refusal) (./some unknown)
    | ./some said.reason
  + act
    ' Does what the rules ask. It sends each packet the foot made to its peer's
    ' address, and puts each change and each request for a new engine in the
    ' foot's mailbox.
    \ endpoint=nat links=row[mesa_wire/link] does=row[mesa_foot/effect]
    ^ nat
    | does.fold 0
      \ ;done=nat effect=mesa_foot/effect
      ^ nat
      ? effect
       > (./send to packet)
        = found links.keep((\ item=mesa_wire/link (and (eq item.id to) (gt item.address 0))))
        ? !(found.len) done
        ; (MesaSend endpoint to found.at(0).gen packet)
        done.inc
       > (./admit request change)
        ; (Send 0 (mesa_wire/wish request change))
        done.inc
       > (./renew era)
        ; (Send 0 (mesa_wire/again era))
        done.inc
  + mark
    ' The rift of a world, the highest epoch it announced, and the lowest key
    ' manifest revision it accepts.
    : rift=nat top=nat floor=nat
  + marked
    ' The mark of a world. Zeros for a world that never started: there is no
    ' mark and Mesa has no manifest for it. None in every other case without a
    ' whole mark: the file is there but is not a mark, or cannot be read, or is
    ' gone although the world started before. Zeros there would let the world
    ' reuse a version it already published.
    \ file=str ring=str
    ^ maybe[mesa_wire/mark]
    = ;bytes (mesa_wire/took file)
      ;there (? (eq 0 bytes) (Stamp file) 0)
      ;begun (? (eq 0 bytes) (Stamp (str/cat_all [ring ".manifest"])) 0)
    ? (and (eq 0 bytes) (and (eq 0 there) (eq 0 begun))) (./some (mesa_wire/mark 0 0 0))
    ? !(eq (wid bytes) 25) .none
    | ./some (mesa_wire/mark (loadvar 0 8 bytes) (loadvar 8 8 bytes) (loadvar 16 8 bytes))
  + resumed
    ' The mark of a world that is starting, from its saved mark and the epoch
    ' the world is at. A world that is behind what it announced was restored to
    ' an older copy. Its rift goes up, so every version it publishes from now
    ' on is later than every version it published before (net/stamp).
    \ was=mesa_wire/mark top=nat
    ^ mesa_wire/mark
    | mesa_wire/mark (? (lt top was.top) was.rift.inc was.rift) (nmax was.top top) was.floor
  + remark
    ' Writes a mark. 1 when the mark is whole on disk (the runtime writes a new
    ' file and then renames it), 0 when it is not.
    \ file=str rift=nat top=nat floor=nat
    ^ nat
    = w64 (bex 64)
      body (add (add (mod rift w64) (lsh (mod top w64) 64)) (lsh (mod floor w64) 128))
    | MesaPersist (mesa_wire/spelled file) (add body (bex 192))
  + halt
    ' Says why the foot does not run, and stops it.
    \ why=str file=str
    ^ nat
    ; (Trace [why file] 0)
    0
  + named
    ' The path of a file as the foot's record gives it, or the default path
    ' when the record gives none.
    \ said=str kept=str
    ^ str
    ? (eq 0 said.len) kept
    said
  + took
    ' The bytes a file holds, or no bytes.
    \ file=str
    ^ nat
    = ;held (Try ReadFile file)
    ? held
     > (./err _) 0
     > (./ok bytes) bytes
  + address
    ' The address where a world is reached. Whoever started the world left it
    ' for the foot in a file, as the one line `host port`. The port is 0 when
    ' the file has no such line. A world gets its address at every start, as it
    ' gets its founding at its first, so a world started somewhere else says
    ' where it is by itself.
    \ handed=nat
    ^ [host=str port=nat]
    = nothing=str ""
      none=[host=str port=nat] [nothing 0]
    ? (lt (wid handed) 2) none
    = text (str/from_atom (mod handed (bex (mul 8 (dec (wid handed))))))
      parts (str/split_byte 32 text)
    ? !(eq 2 parts.len) none
    ?> (./some port) (nat/parse parts.at(1)) none
    = got=[host=str port=nat] [parts.at(0) port]
    got
  + kept
    ' The bytes of a file Mesa keeps for the world, or 0 when there is no file.
    ' `whole` is false when the file is there but cannot be read: the foot must
    ' then stop, and not start as if there were no file.
    \ file=str
    ^ [whole=bool bytes=nat]
    = ;bytes (mesa_wire/took file)
      ;there (? (eq 0 bytes) (Stamp file) 0)
    [(eq 0 there) bytes]
  + told
    ' The text of a reason Mesa gave.
    \ why=nat
    ^ str
    | str/from_atom (mod why (bex (mul 8 (dec (wid why)))))
  + spelled
    ' A text as bytes, for the Mesa bridge.
    \ text=str
    ^ nat
    | mesa_foot/tag (str/to_atom text)
  + beside
    ' A file Mesa keeps beside the world's key file, as bytes for the bridge:
    ' the key manifest, or the authority checkpoint.
    \ ring=str what=str
    ^ nat
    | mesa_wire/spelled (str/cat_all [ring "." what])
  + ring_of
    ' The file of the world's key at a life. The first key is in the ring file.
    ' Each later key has a file of its own.
    \ ring=str life=nat
    ^ str
    ? (le life 1) ring
    | str/cat_all [ring "." (nat/show life)]
  + revision
    ' The key manifest revision an activation made, or 0 when the keys were not
    ' activated.
    \ acts=row[row[nat]]
    ^ nat
    | acts.fold 0
      \ out=nat act=row[nat]
      ^ nat
      ? (eq 6 act.at(0)) act.at(1)
      out
  + admit
    ' Asks Mesa to accept what a card names for a peer. 0 when Mesa holds that
    ' key, otherwise the reason it refused. Mesa refuses a lower life or rift,
    ' and a different key at the same life. A peer whose card was removed is
    ' blocked, and only a card with a higher life lifts the block.
    \ authority=nat file=nat want=mesa_wire/route
    ^ nat
    = now (div (Now 0) 1000000)
      ;stood (MesaStanding authority want.id)
      blocked (eq 1 stood.at(5))
    ? (and blocked (le want.life stood.at(2))) (mesa_foot/tag "Blocked")
    = ;lifted (? blocked (MesaBlock authority file now want.id 0) 0)
    | MesaVouch authority file now want.id mesa_foot/domain want.life want.rift want.key
  + denied
    ' The write that records a card Mesa refused: the key the card names, and
    ' the reason. It goes beside the card, where this world keeps where the
    ' peer's root stands. No write when the record already says so.
    \ self=iota want=mesa_wire/route why=nat state=namespace
    ^ row[mesa_foot/effect]
    = card=path [self 'io 'mesa want.world 'stand]
      none=row[mesa_foot/effect] []
      text (mesa_wire/told why)
      was (sovereign_care .x card state).fil.fall(myth/new)
    ? (and (eq want.key was.nat_at(['barred] 0)) (equal[str] text was.txt_at(['cause]))) none
    = said=myth (myth/sing ['barred] (pails/n want.key)).put(['cause] (pails/t text))
      change (? (net/live card state) (writ/poke said) (writ/make said))
    | none.snoc((mesa_foot/effect/admit 0 (mesa_foot/change/write card change)))
  + locked
    ' What this world shares with a peer, or none when Mesa does not serve that
    ' peer.
    \ keys=nat authority=nat id=nat
    ^ row[mesa_foot/lock]
    = none=row[mesa_foot/lock] []
      ;stood (MesaStanding authority id)
    ? !(eq 1 stood.at(4)) none
    = ;seal (MesaLock keys authority id (mesa_foot/tag "seal"))
      ;nonce (MesaLock keys authority id (mesa_foot/tag "nonce"))
      ;name (MesaLock keys authority id (mesa_foot/tag "name"))
    | none.snoc((mesa_foot/lock id seal nonce name))
  + fed
    ' What the foot holds after it told Mesa the cards: the links, what the
    ' world shares with each peer, what the engine reported (reads that
    ' stopped), and the writes that record what Mesa refused.
    : links=row[mesa_wire/link] locks=row[mesa_foot/lock] acts=row[row[nat]] notes=row[mesa_foot/effect]
  + feed
    ' Brings Mesa in line with the cards, then gives the engine and the socket
    ' what Mesa holds.
    ' - new or changed card: ask Mesa to accept its key (mesa_wire/admit) and
    '   give the engine the answer
    ' - new address: set the peer's route
    ' - card gone: block the peer
    ' - unchanged card: nothing
    \ wanted=row[mesa_wire/route] links=row[mesa_wire/link] keys=nat authority=nat file=nat state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ mesa_wire/fed
    = no_links=row[mesa_wire/link] []
      no_locks=row[mesa_foot/lock] []
      no_acts=row[row[nat]] []
      no_notes=row[mesa_foot/effect] []
      nowhere=str ""
      ;kept
        | wanted.fold (mesa_wire/fed no_links no_locks no_acts no_notes)
          \ ;out=mesa_wire/fed want=mesa_wire/route
          ^ mesa_wire/fed
          = had links.keep((\ item=mesa_wire/link (eq item.id want.id)))
            old (? (gt had.len 0) had.at(0) (mesa_wire/link want.world want.id 0 0 0 nowhere 0 0 0))
            same (and (eq old.key want.key) (and (eq old.life want.life) (eq old.rift want.rift)))
            ;why (? same 0 (mesa_wire/admit authority file want))
          ? !(eq 0 why) (out.set_links(out.links.snoc(old.set_key(0))).set_notes(out.notes.weld((mesa_wire/denied state.self want why state))))
          = one=row[nat] [want.id]
            ;synced (? same no_acts (MesaSync authority foot.engine foot.endpoint one))
            placed (and (equal[str] old.host want.host) (eq old.port want.port))
            ;address (? placed old.address (MesaResolve (mesa_wire/spelled want.host) want.port))
            ;routed (? (placed || (eq 0 address)) 0 (MesaRoute foot.engine foot.endpoint want.id old.gen old.gen.inc address))
            next (mesa_wire/link want.world want.id want.key want.life want.rift (? routed want.host old.host) (? routed want.port old.port) (? routed address old.address) (? routed old.gen.inc old.gen))
            before foot.locks.keep((\ item=mesa_foot/lock (eq item.id want.id)))
            ;shared (? (and same (gt before.len 0)) before (mesa_wire/locked keys authority want.id))
          | out.set_links(out.links.snoc(next)).set_locks(out.locks.weld(shared)).set_acts(out.acts.weld(synced))
      now (div (Now 0) 1000000)
    | links.fold kept
      \ ;out=mesa_wire/fed item=mesa_wire/link
      ^ mesa_wire/fed
      ? (wanted.any((\ want=mesa_wire/route (eq want.id item.id)))) out
      ? (eq 0 item.key) (out.set_links(out.links.snoc(item)))
      = one=row[nat] [item.id]
        ;barred (MesaBlock authority file now item.id 1)
        ;synced (MesaSync authority foot.engine foot.endpoint one)
      | out.set_links(out.links.snoc(item.set_key(0))).set_acts(out.acts.weld(synced))
  + socket
    ' A socket, and the number a waiter waits on it by.
    : endpoint=nat fd=nat
  + bind
    ' Makes the foot's socket on a port (0: the operating system picks one) and
    ' gives it the routes of the links, at the generations the engine knows.
    \ port=nat links=row[mesa_wire/link]
    ^ mesa_wire/socket
    = limits mesa_foot/limits
      ;endpoint (MesaEndpoint (mesa_wire/spelled (str/cat_all ["0.0.0.0:" (nat/show port)])) limits.at(0))
      ;fd (MesaSocket endpoint)
      ;tracked
        | links.fold 0
          \ ;done=nat item=mesa_wire/link
          ^ nat
          ? (eq 0 item.address) done
          ; (MesaTrack endpoint item.id 0 item.gen item.address)
          done.inc
    | mesa_wire/socket endpoint fd
  + drive
    ' An engine, what it reported while starting, and the key manifest revision
    ' (0: Mesa did not activate the key, and the engine is closed).
    : engine=nat acts=row[row[nat]] floor=nat
  + engine
    ' Makes the foot's engine. It starts closed, with no key. Mesa then
    ' activates the world's key for it: the manifest is on disk before the
    ' engine signs anything. The engine gets what Mesa holds of each peer and
    ' the routes the socket has.
    \ self=iota life=nat links=row[mesa_wire/link] endpoint=nat keys=nat authority=nat manifest=nat bounds=row[nat]
    ^ mesa_wire/drive
    = none=row[nat] []
      ;engine (MesaEngine (mesa_foot/id self) mesa_foot/domain mesa_foot/limits bounds)
      ;acts (MesaActivate keys authority engine endpoint manifest life)
      ids
        | links.fold none
          \ out=row[nat] item=mesa_wire/link
          ^ row[nat]
          | out.snoc(item.id)
      ;synced (MesaSync authority engine endpoint ids)
      ;attached
        | links.fold 0
          \ ;done=nat item=mesa_wire/link
          ^ nat
          ? (eq 0 item.address) done
          ; (MesaAttach engine endpoint item.id item.gen)
          done.inc
    | mesa_wire/drive engine acts.weld(synced) (mesa_wire/revision acts)
  + sweep
    ' Retires every key of the world before the current one and removes its
    ' file. Normally there is none. A world that stopped between activating a
    ' new key and retiring the old one has one, and this finishes that key
    ' change. It gives the manifest revision after the last retirement, or 0
    ' when it retired nothing. Mesa closes the engine for a retirement, so the
    ' caller activates the key again when the answer is not 0.
    \ ring=str life=nat keys=nat authority=nat manifest=nat
    ^ nat
    % version=nat 1
      last=nat 0
    ^ nat
    ? (ge version life) last
    = ;done (MesaRetire keys authority manifest version (mesa_wire/spelled (mesa_wire/ring_of ring version)))
    | _ version.inc (nmax last done)
  + renew
    ' Gives the foot a new engine on the same socket and closes the old one.
    ' The foot asks for this when its engine has no room left for a page. The
    ' new engine holds no page. A name always has the same content, so the new
    ' engine binds the same bytes when a reader asks again. The answer is the
    ' turn of the new foot and the key manifest revision. The revision is 0
    ' when Mesa did not activate the key for the new engine: the foot then
    ' keeps its old engine.
    \ life=nat links=row[mesa_wire/link] keys=nat authority=nat manifest=nat bounds=row[nat] state=namespace foot=mesa_foot/foot
    ^ [turn=mesa_foot/turn floor=nat]
    = ;made (mesa_wire/engine state.self life links foot.endpoint keys authority manifest bounds)
      ;shut (MesaClose (? (eq 0 made.floor) made.engine foot.engine))
    ? (eq 0 made.floor) [(mesa_foot/quiet foot) 0]
    [(mesa_foot/acted made.acts state (mesa_foot/raised made.engine foot)) made.floor]
  + turned
    ' The answer to a change of the world's key: whether Mesa changed it, the
    ' new public key, what the engine reported, and the key manifest revision.
    : ok=nat public=nat acts=row[row[nat]] floor=nat
  + rotate
    ' Changes the world's key to the key of a higher life. Mesa makes the new
    ' key in a file of its own, accepts it for this world, and signs with it
    ' from then on. Then Mesa retires the old key and its file is removed. Mesa
    ' closes the engine at every manifest change, so the new key is activated
    ' a second time after the retirement.
    \ self=iota ring=str old=nat new=nat endpoint=nat engine=nat keys=nat authority=nat
    ^ mesa_wire/turned
    = me (mesa_foot/id self)
      none=row[row[nat]] []
      failed (mesa_wire/turned 0 0 none 0)
      manifest (mesa_wire/beside ring "manifest")
      ;got (MesaKeyImport keys (mesa_wire/spelled (mesa_wire/ring_of ring new)) new new 0 1)
    ? !(eq 2 got.len) failed
    = ;why (MesaVouch authority (mesa_wire/beside ring "authority") (div (Now 0) 1000000) me mesa_foot/domain new 0 got.at(0))
    ? !(eq 0 why) failed
    = ;first (MesaActivate keys authority engine endpoint manifest new)
    ? (eq 0 (mesa_wire/revision first)) (mesa_wire/turned 0 0 first 0)
    = ;retired (MesaRetire keys authority manifest old (mesa_wire/spelled (mesa_wire/ring_of ring old)))
      ;second (MesaActivate keys authority engine endpoint manifest new)
      floor (mesa_wire/revision second)
    ? (eq 0 floor) (mesa_wire/turned 0 0 first.weld(second) 0)
    | mesa_wire/turned 1 got.at(0) first.weld(second) floor
  + up
    ' A foot that started: the foot, its links, the handles on the keys and the
    ' authority Mesa keeps for the world, the number of its socket, its key
    ' manifest revision, the life and public key of the key Mesa signs with,
    ' and what the rules ask for at the start. `why` is empty for a foot that
    ' started. Otherwise it is the reason the foot did not start.
    : why=str foot=mesa_foot/foot links=row[mesa_wire/link] keys=nat authority=nat fd=nat floor=nat life=nat public=nat does=row[mesa_foot/effect]
  + down
    ' The answer of a foot that did not start, with the reason.
    \ why=str rift=nat life=nat world=namespace
    ^ mesa_wire/up
    = no_links=row[mesa_wire/link] []
      no_does=row[mesa_foot/effect] []
    | mesa_wire/up why (mesa_foot/start world.self rift 0 0) no_links 0 0 0 0 life 0 no_does
  + raise
    ' Starts a foot. It opens what Mesa keeps for the world beside the ring
    ' file (the authority and the keys), makes the world's key the first time
    ' (if the record states none), asks Mesa to accept that key for the world,
    ' makes the socket and the engine, and then tells Mesa the cards.
    '
    ' The foot does not start when a file Mesa keeps is damaged, cannot be
    ' read, or is older than the mark allows. It gives the reason. It never
    ' starts as if the file were missing: that would give the world a new
    ' identity or let an old key back in.
    '
    ' The life of the key is the higher of the life the caller wants and the
    ' life Mesa holds for the world. So a world restored to an old record does
    ' not go back to an old key.
    \ ring=str port=nat rift=nat floor=nat wanted=nat stated=bool routes=row[mesa_wire/route] began=nat bounds=row[nat] world=namespace
    ^ mesa_wire/up
    = me (mesa_foot/id world.self)
      no_links=row[mesa_wire/link] []
      no_acts=row[row[nat]] []
      started=str ""
      held (mesa_wire/beside ring "authority")
      kept_at (mesa_wire/beside ring "manifest")
      ;fresh (Entropy 16)
      incarnation (add 1 (mod fresh (bex 120)))
      ;[trusted checkpoint] (mesa_wire/kept (str/cat_all [ring ".authority"]))
      ;[listed manifest] (mesa_wire/kept (str/cat_all [ring ".manifest"]))
    ? !(trusted) (mesa_wire/down "the file of the authority cannot be read" rift wanted world)
    ? !(listed) (mesa_wire/down "the manifest of the keys cannot be read" rift wanted world)
    = ;unfit (MesaAuthorityFit incarnation checkpoint)
    ? !(eq 0 unfit) (mesa_wire/down (str/cat_all ["Mesa does not take the file of the authority: " (mesa_wire/told unfit)]) rift wanted world)
    = ;unkept (MesaKeysFit me mesa_foot/domain incarnation.inc 1 manifest floor)
    ? !(eq 0 unkept) (mesa_wire/down (str/cat_all ["Mesa does not take the manifest of the keys: " (mesa_wire/told unkept)]) rift wanted world)
    = ;authority (MesaAuthority incarnation checkpoint held mesa_foot/domain began)
      ;keys (MesaKeys me mesa_foot/domain incarnation.inc 1 manifest floor)
      ;stood (MesaStanding authority me)
      life (nmax wanted stood.at(2))
      ;got (MesaKeyImport keys (mesa_wire/spelled (mesa_wire/ring_of ring life)) life life 0 (? stated 0 1))
    ? !(eq 2 got.len) (mesa_wire/down "the file of the key is not there or is not a key, and the record states a key" rift life world)
    = ;why (MesaVouch authority held began me mesa_foot/domain life 0 got.at(0))
    ? !(eq 0 why) (mesa_wire/down (str/cat_all ["Mesa does not accept the key of this world: " (mesa_wire/told why)]) rift life world)
    = ;sock (mesa_wire/bind port no_links)
      ;made (mesa_wire/engine world.self life no_links sock.endpoint keys authority kept_at bounds)
    ? (eq 0 made.floor) (mesa_wire/down "Mesa did not activate the key of this world" rift life world)
    = ;swept (mesa_wire/sweep ring life keys authority kept_at)
      ;again (? (eq 0 swept) no_acts (MesaActivate keys authority made.engine sock.endpoint kept_at life))
      level (? (eq 0 swept) made.floor (mesa_wire/revision again))
    ? (eq 0 level) (mesa_wire/down "Mesa did not activate the key of this world after it retired an old key" rift life world)
    = begun (mesa_foot/start world.self rift made.engine sock.endpoint)
      ;fed (mesa_wire/feed routes no_links keys authority held world begun)
      met (mesa_foot/meet (mesa_wire/peers fed.links) fed.locks begun)
      ;opening
        | mesa_foot/after (mesa_foot/acted made.acts.weld(again).weld(fed.acts) world met)
          \ ready=mesa_foot/foot
          ^ mesa_foot/turn
          | mesa_foot/tick began world ready
    | mesa_wire/up started opening.foot fed.links keys authority sock.fd level life got.at(0) fed.notes.weld(opening.does)
  + run
    ' The foot. It waits for the world as it is now and reads its mark. It
    ' raises its rift when the world is behind what it announced before. Then
    ' it starts (mesa_wire/raise) and runs the rules on everything that
    ' arrives.
    '
    ' The foot listens at the address it is given at start (io/mesa/address)
    ' and writes that address on its record. Given none, it listens where its
    ' record says. When a port appears on a record that had none, the foot
    ' makes a socket on that port then. A foot keeps its port until it stops.
    '
    ' When Mesa holds a later key for the world than the record states, the
    ' foot writes the life and key Mesa holds on the record.
    \ init=feet/task/init self=nat
    ^ nat
    = record (mesa_wire/own init.ax)
      ;handed (mesa_wire/took "io/mesa/address")
    = [host given] (mesa_wire/address handed)
    = port (? (eq 0 given) record.nat_at(['port] 0) given)
      ring (mesa_wire/named record.txt_at(['ring]) "io/mesa/ring")
      file (mesa_wire/named record.txt_at(['mark]) "io/mesa/mark")
      ;folder (Folder "io/mesa")
    ; (mesa_wire/look init.parent)
    = ;world
        % ignored=nat 0
        ^ namespace
        = ;[message caps] (Recv[mesa_wire/task] 0)
        ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
        ?> (./binary request status body mime) message (_ 0)
        | mesa_wire/world body
      ;found (mesa_wire/marked file ring)
    ?> (./some was) found (mesa_wire/halt "mesa foot: the mark is not whole or is gone, and the foot does not run" file)
    = resumed (mesa_wire/resumed was world.local.top)
      rift resumed.rift
      seen resumed.top
      ;noted (mesa_wire/remark file rift seen was.floor)
    ? !(noted) (mesa_wire/halt "mesa foot: the mark was not written, and the foot does not run" file)
    = began (div (Now 0) 1000000)
      held (mesa_wire/beside ring "authority")
      kept_at (mesa_wire/beside ring "manifest")
      ;up (mesa_wire/raise ring port rift was.floor record.nat_at(['life] 1) (gt record.nat_at(['key] 0) 0) (mesa_wire/routes init.ax) began mesa_foot/bounds world)
    ? (gt up.why.len 0) (mesa_wire/halt (str/cat_all ["mesa foot: " up.why]) ring)
    = ;kept (mesa_wire/remark file rift seen up.floor)
      keys up.keys
      authority up.authority
    ? !(kept) (mesa_wire/halt "mesa foot: the mark was not written, and the foot does not run" file)
    ; (mesa_wire/watch up.fd 1)
    ; (? (and (eq record.nat_at(['key] 0) up.public) (eq record.nat_at(['life] 1) up.life)) 0 (Send 0 (mesa_wire/note [world.self 'io 'mesa] ((myth/sing ['key] (pails/n up.public)).put(['life] (pails/n up.life))))))
    ; (? ((eq 0 given) || (and (eq given record.nat_at(['port] 0)) (equal[str] host record.txt_at(['host])))) 0 (Send 0 (mesa_wire/note [world.self 'io 'mesa] (myth/sing ['port] (pails/n given)).put(['host] (pails/t host)))))
    ; (Trace ["mesa foot listening" port] 0)
    ; (mesa_wire/act up.foot.endpoint up.links up.does)
    % foot=mesa_foot/foot up.foot
      view=namespace world
      links=row[mesa_wire/link] up.links
      top=nat seen
      floor=nat up.floor
      last=nat began
      own_life=nat up.life
      at=nat port
      serial=nat 1
      stopping=nat 0
      queue=row[mesa_wire/wish] []
    = ;[message caps] (Recv[mesa_wire/task] 0)
      ticked
        ? message
         > time=mesa_wire/tick .true
        .false
    ; (? ticked 0 (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps))
    ? message
     > wanted=mesa_wire/wish
      ; (? (queue.len) 0 (mesa_wire/ask init.parent [wanted]))
      | _ foot view links top floor last own_life at serial stopping queue.snoc(wanted)
     > (./binary request status body mime)
      = held (mesa_wire/world body)
        no=maybe[iota] .none
        ;refusal (? (eq 1 request) (mesa_wire/plan init.parent queue held) no)
        refused (maybe/is_some refusal)
        rest (? refused queue.drop(1) queue)
        ;answered (? refused (mesa_foot/landed queue.at(0).request refusal held foot) (mesa_foot/quiet foot))
      ; (? refused (mesa_wire/ask init.parent rest) 0)
      ; (mesa_wire/act foot.endpoint links answered.does)
      ? (eq held.local.top view.local.top) (_ answered.foot held links top floor last own_life at serial stopping rest)
      = ;turn (mesa_foot/turned held answered.foot)
        higher (nmax top held.local.top)
        ;kept (? (gt higher top) (mesa_wire/remark file foot.rift higher floor) 1)
      ; (? kept 0 (Trace ["mesa foot: the mark was not written, and the foot announces nothing" file] 0))
      ? !(kept) (_ answered.foot held links top floor last own_life at serial stopping rest)
      ; (mesa_wire/act foot.endpoint links turn.does)
      | _ turn.foot held links higher floor last own_life at serial stopping rest
     > (./fact binding)
      ; (mesa_wire/look init.parent)
      ? (mesa_wire/stopped binding) (_ foot view links top floor last own_life at serial 1 queue)
      = card (mesa_wire/own binding)
        wish card.nat_at(['port] 0)
        opens (and (eq 0 at) (gt wish 0))
        ;sock (? opens (mesa_wire/bind wish links) (mesa_wire/socket foot.endpoint 0))
        ;shut (? opens (MesaClose foot.endpoint) 0)
        port_now (? opens wish at)
        serial_now (? opens serial.inc serial)
      ; (? opens (mesa_wire/watch sock.fd serial_now) 0)
      ; (? opens (Trace ["mesa foot listening" wish] 0) 0)
      = placed foot.set_endpoint(sock.endpoint)
        no_acts=row[row[nat]] []
        no_locks=row[mesa_foot/lock] []
        next_life card.nat_at(['life] 1)
        ;turned (? (gt next_life own_life) (mesa_wire/rotate view.self ring own_life next_life placed.endpoint placed.engine keys authority) (mesa_wire/turned 0 0 no_acts 0))
        life_now (? turned.ok next_life own_life)
        floor_now (? turned.ok turned.floor floor)
      ; (? turned.ok (mesa_wire/remark file placed.rift top floor_now) 0)
      ; (? turned.ok (Send 0 (mesa_wire/note [view.self 'io 'mesa] (myth/sing ['key] (pails/n turned.public)))) 0)
      ; (? (and (gt next_life own_life) !(turned.ok)) (Trace ["mesa foot: the key of this world was not changed" next_life] 0) 0)
      = base (? turned.ok placed.set_locks(no_locks) placed)
        ;fed (mesa_wire/feed (mesa_wire/routes binding) links keys authority held view base)
        met (mesa_foot/meet (mesa_wire/peers fed.links) fed.locks base)
        ;turn (mesa_foot/acted turned.acts.weld(fed.acts) view met)
      ; (mesa_wire/act met.endpoint fed.links fed.notes)
      ; (mesa_wire/act met.endpoint fed.links turn.does)
      | _ turn.foot view fed.links top floor_now last life_now port_now serial_now stopping queue
     > time=mesa_wire/tick
      ? !(eq time.serial serial)
        ; (Send caps.at(0) 0)
        ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
        | _ foot view links top floor last own_life at serial stopping queue
      ? (gt stopping 0)
        ; (Send caps.at(0) 0)
        ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
        ; (MesaClose foot.endpoint)
        ; (MesaClose foot.engine)
        0
      = ;came (MesaHear foot.endpoint)
        packets=row[row[nat]] came
        start=mesa_foot/turn (mesa_foot/quiet foot)
        ;heard
          | packets.fold start
            \ ;acc=mesa_foot/turn packet=row[nat]
            ^ mesa_foot/turn
            | mesa_foot/after acc
              \ ready=mesa_foot/foot
              ^ mesa_foot/turn
              | mesa_foot/heard packet.at(0) packet.at(1) packet.at(2) view ready
      ; (mesa_wire/act foot.endpoint links heard.does)
      = due (ge time.now (add last mesa_foot/every))
        ;moved (? due (mesa_foot/tick time.now view heard.foot) (mesa_foot/clock time.now view heard.foot))
      ; (mesa_wire/act foot.endpoint links moved.does)
      = ;next (MesaDeadline foot.engine foot.endpoint)
        ahead (? (le next time.now) 1 (sub next time.now))
        wait
          ? (eq packets.len 64) 1
          ? (eq 0 next) 1000
          ? (gt ahead 1000) 1000
          ahead
      ; (Send caps.at(0) wait)
      ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
      | _ moved.foot view links top floor (? due time.now last) own_life at serial stopping queue
     > asked=mesa_wire/again
      ? !(eq asked.era foot.era) (_ foot view links top floor last own_life at serial stopping queue)
      = ;[turn level] (mesa_wire/renew own_life links keys authority kept_at mesa_foot/bounds view foot)
      ? (eq 0 level)
        ; (Trace ["mesa foot: a new engine was not made" own_life] 0)
        | _ foot view links top floor last own_life at serial stopping queue
      = ;kept (mesa_wire/remark file foot.rift top level)
      ; (mesa_wire/act turn.foot.endpoint links turn.does)
      | _ turn.foot view links top level last own_life at serial stopping queue
     > (./ack err)
      ? !(queue.len) (_ foot view links top floor last own_life at serial stopping queue)
      = ;turn (mesa_foot/landed queue.at(0).request (mesa_wire/why err) view foot)
        rest queue.drop(1)
      ; (mesa_wire/act foot.endpoint links turn.does)
      ; (mesa_wire/ask init.parent rest)
      ; (mesa_wire/look init.parent)
      | _ turn.foot view links top floor last own_life at serial stopping rest
    | _ foot view links top floor last own_life at serial stopping queue
  + stopped
    ' True if the foot's record says the foot must stop: the record is gone or
    ' holds `stop`.
    \ binding=axal[saga]
    ^ bool
    ?> (./some version) binding.fil .true
    | gt (unpin version.myth).nat_at(['stop] 0) 0
  + accepted
    ' True if the supervisor accepted a write or a registration.
    \ reply=feet/task[unit]
    ^ bool
    ? reply
     > (./ack err)
      ? err
       > .none .true
       > (./some _) .false
    .false
  + submit
    ' Sends one write and says whether the world accepted it.
    \ server=nat target=path change=writ
    ^ bool
    ; (SendCaps server (helm/card/step target change) [0])
    = ;[reply caps] (Recv[feet/task[unit]] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
    | mesa_wire/accepted reply
  + present
    ' Makes an empty record for the foot if the world has none. It leaves an
    ' existing record alone: the port, the key and everything else on it stay.
    ' An empty poke changes nothing, and the world refuses one only when there
    ' is no record. A make would replace the record.
    \ server=nat target=path
    ^ bool
    ? (mesa_wire/submit server target (writ/poke myth/new)) .true
    | mesa_wire/submit server target (writ/make myth/new)
  + unseated
    ' The writes that give /<self>/our its hand, for a world that lacks it. The
    ' hand tells the foot of news (net/herald, net/watch). That name must hold
    ' a record: the kernel counts changes only below a name that holds one.
    '
    ' No write for what is already there, so a world that starts again makes no
    ' event.
    \ self=iota state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      ours=path [self 'our]
      held (\ name=path (sovereign_care .x name state).fil)
      handed
        \ name=path
        ^ bool
        ?> (./some record) (held name) .false
        | maybe/is_some record.get(limb_slot)
      one (? (maybe/is_some (held (net/horn self))) none none.snoc([(net/horn self) (writ/make (form/card net/herald (lore/line "Tells the Mesa foot of news")))]))
    ? (handed ours) one
    ? (maybe/is_some (held ours)) one.snoc([ours (writ/poke (net/watch self))])
    | one.snoc([ours (writ/make (net/watch self))])
  + seat
    ' Gives /<self>/our its hand if it lacks it (mesa_wire/unseated).
    \ server=nat self=iota
    ^ bool
    ; (SendCaps server (helm/card/snapshot_bat 0 mesa_wire/whole) [0])
    = ;[reply caps] (Recv[feet/task[unit]] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
    ?> (./binary request status body mime) reply .false
    | (mesa_wire/unseated self (mesa_wire/world body)).all((\ [name change] (mesa_wire/submit server name change)))
  + start
    ' Starts the foot of a world: makes sure the record /<self>/io/mesa is
    ' there and /<self>/our has its hand, and registers the foot at that path.
    ' A world calls this once, when it starts. The mesa mount is the switch
    ' that makes a world call it.
    \ server=nat self=iota arguments=row[str]
    ^ nat
    = home=path [self 'io 'mesa]
    ? !(mesa_wire/present server home)
      (error (pails/t "Mesa foot record refused"))
    ? !(mesa_wire/seat server self)
      (error (pails/t "Mesa herald refused"))
    = registration | helm/supervisor/register home mesa_wire/run
    ; (SendCaps server registration [0])
    = ;[reply caps] | Recv[feet/task[unit]] 0
    ; | helm/supervisor/close_caps caps
    ? !(mesa_wire/accepted reply)
      (error (pails/t "Mesa foot registration failed"))
    0
